      {
        "id": "tipping-points",
        "title": "Tipping points",
        "layout": "split",
        "align": "left",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "body": "Sometimes an ecosystem cannot go back after a certain point. An Amazon rainforest that has dried out, or a coral reef that has died, does not simply recover. We call this a tipping point: a limit after which the change can no longer be stopped."
          }
        ],
        "aside": [
